<<case "meek">>
	"I.. um, thank you," you murmur, cheeks warming, unsure where to look.
	<<He>> just beams at you, entirely unbothered by your fluster.
<<case "shy">>
	"I.. um, thank you," you say, cheeks warming as you look down at your shoes.
	<<He>> just beams at you, entirely unbothered by your fluster.
<<case "polite">>
	"Thank you, that's very kind of you," you say, a little pink in the cheeks.
	<<He>> just beams at you, delighted.
<<case "confident">>
	"Thank you," you say warmly, meeting <<his>> eyes. "I appreciate it." <<His>> smile widens.
<<case "bratty">>
	"Obviously," you say, though the compliment still tugs a smile out of you despite yourself.
	<<He>> laughs, delighted rather than put off.
<<case "docile">>
	"Th-thank you," you say softly, cheeks warming, a smile tugging at your mouth.
	<<He>> just beams at you.
<<case "flamboyant">>
	"Thank you, you're too kind," you say with a small flourish, cheeks warming.
	<<He>> just beams at you, delighted.
<<case "cruel">>
	"Obviously," you say with a shrug, though the compliment still tugs a smile out of you despite yourself.
	<<He>> laughs, delighted rather than put off.
<<default>>
	"Thank you," you say warmly, and mean it. <<His>> smile widens, as if your words alone were a gift.
<</switch>>
